35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The basin survived; the apron didn’t. And the fund won’t pay for paving. We’re building a garden, not a plaza.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The hoarding limits are clear. The southern ground can be staged, but the centre and gate cannot. This dictates our phasing.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, triple the cost! And only seven staff left? That’s terrifying. @Asuka, how are you managing with so few people?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"Seven staff cannot cover this. The bought-in services are a stopgap, not a solution. We need a plan that doesn’t rely on ghosts.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The data is clear. Drainage failures doubled, and heat spikes are severe. People stick to firm ground. We must design for that reality, not against it.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Misaki, your phasing constraints align with my findings. If the fund excludes hard surfaces, we must prioritize planting. Let’s not waste money on pavement that will crack.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"Benjamin, the planting record is grim. Half died from neglect. We need a contractor who guarantees aftercare, not just digging.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, that’s so sad! But wait, if planting costs triple, maybe we should focus on hard surfaces? I’m worried about the budget!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"Mio, hard surfaces are cheaper now, but they fail later. With seven staff, we cannot maintain complex planting. We need a design that survives neglect, not one that demands constant care.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"Asuka is right. The heat and drainage data prove complex planting will fail. We need robust, low-maintenance species that tolerate the actual ground conditions, not idealized designs.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Mio, hard surfaces are exactly what the fund forbids. We can’t pave what we can’t afford. Focus on the planting that actually survives.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"Mio, the fund excludes hard surfaces. We must plant, but only with guaranteed aftercare. The eastern avenue proves neglect kills trees.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, I’m so confused! If planting is expensive and hard surfaces are banned, what is left? I’m scared the city can’t afford this!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"Mio, the answer is simplicity. We choose low-maintenance species that survive neglect. We cannot afford complex care with seven staff.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,"Mio, the ground dictates the design. We need species that handle the heat and drainage failures. Simplicity is not a compromise; it is the only viable path forward.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"Mio, breathe. The fund pays for water and plants. We choose species that ignore neglect. No pavement, no panic. Just resilient green.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"Mio, the phasing allows the south to work while the park stays open. We just need a firm that won’t vanish.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, resilient green sounds lovely! But with only seven staff, who actually waters it? I’m still worried about those triple costs!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"Mio, the casual pool handles weekends. We need a design that requires minimal intervention. If it needs daily attention, it will die.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,"Mio, the drainage data confirms it. We need plants that thrive in wet, hot conditions. Simplicity is survival, not a budget cut.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
